––– comment –––
Shared bulk_import into a shard table with local and agent targets on two daemons: the coordinator
starts, feeds, commits and cancels the pool of a remote target with the command SHARD_BULK;
any failed remote call fails the whole load, and
PURGE BULK_IMPORT by the shard table name cancels the pools on every node. Both daemons get
threads = 8 for any CPU count of the runner.
––– input –––
sed 's/^searchd {/searchd {\n\tthreads = 8/' test/clt-tests/base/searchd-with-flexible-ports.conf > /tmp/two.conf; chmod +x /tmp/two.conf; cat > /tmp/rb.sh <<'EOF'
start() { mkdir -p /var/{run,lib,log}/manticore-$1; rm -f /var/log/manticore-$1/searchd.log; INSTANCE=$1 searchd -c /tmp/two.conf > /dev/null; if timeout 30 grep -qm1 'accepting connections' <(tail -n 1000 -f /var/log/manticore-$1/searchd.log); then echo "node $1 up"; else echo "node $1 failed"; fi; }
stop() { INSTANCE=$1 searchd -c /tmp/two.conf --stopwait > /dev/null; echo "node $1 stopped"; }
sql() { mysql -h0 -P$1 --skip-table --batch --raw --skip-column-names -e "$2"; }
post() { curl -sS -X POST "http://localhost:1308/bulk?bulk_import=$1&shared$2" -H 'Content-Type: application/x-ndjson' --data-binary @"$3" -w ' HTTP %{http_code}\n'; }
commit() { printf '\n' > /tmp/commit.ndjson; post "$1" "$2" /tmp/commit.ndjson; }
gen() { for ((i=$2; i<=$3; i++)); do printf '{"insert":{"table":"%s","id":%d,"doc":{"title":"doc %d","gid":%d}}}\n' "$1" "$i" "$i" "$((i % 7))"; done; }
kids() { echo "children=$(ps -eo args | grep -c '[i]ndexer_rt_bulk_chunk')"; }
counts() { echo "$(sql 1306 "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM $1") = $(sql 1306 "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM ${1}_0") + $(sql 2306 "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM ${1}_1")"; }
vals() { for ((i=$1; i<=$2; i++)); do printf "(%d,'doc %d',%d)" "$i" "$i" "$((i % 7))"; [ "$i" -lt "$2" ] && printf ','; done; }
EOF
––– output –––
––– input –––
source /tmp/rb.sh; start 1; start 2; sql 2306 "CREATE TABLE r_1 (title TEXT, gid INT)"; sql 1306 "CREATE TABLE r_0 (title TEXT, gid INT); CREATE TABLE r (title TEXT, gid INT) type='shard' local='r_0' agent='127.0.0.1:2312:r_1'"
––– output –––
node 1 up
node 2 up
––– comment –––
One load into a local and a remote target: nothing is visible before the commit, each target
runs one child; the commit publishes one chunk on each node, and every row is where an ordinary
write routes its id (REPLACE through the shard table changes no count).
––– input –––
source /tmp/rb.sh; gen r 1 3000 > /tmp/a.ndjson; gen r 3001 6000 > /tmp/b.ndjson; post r '' /tmp/a.ndjson > /tmp/a.reply & post r '' /tmp/b.ndjson > /tmp/b.reply & wait; cat /tmp/a.reply /tmp/b.reply; kids; counts r
