––– comment –––
A replaced shard table object (here by ALTER CLUSTER ... ADD) fails the load at the commit, which
cancels the remote pool; data requests before it go on.
––– input –––
source /tmp/rb.sh; sql 2306 "CREATE TABLE c_1 (title TEXT, gid INT)"; sql 1306 "CREATE TABLE c (title TEXT, gid INT) type='shard' agent='127.0.0.1:2312:c_1'"; gen c 1 30 > /tmp/c.ndjson; post c '' /tmp/c.ndjson; kids; sql 1306 "CREATE CLUSTER cc; ALTER CLUSTER cc ADD c"; post c '' /tmp/c.ndjson; kids; commit c ''; kids; sql 1306 "ALTER CLUSTER cc DROP c; DELETE CLUSTER cc"
