––– comment –––
PURGE BULK_IMPORT by the shard table name on the coordinator: without the option it refuses while
the load is open; with clear_sessions=1 the pools on both nodes are gone and the remote table
takes ordinary writes.
––– input –––
source /tmp/rb.sh; post r '' /tmp/o.ndjson; sql 1306 "PURGE BULK_IMPORT FROM TABLE r"; kids; sql 1306 "PURGE BULK_IMPORT FROM TABLE r OPTION clear_sessions=1"; kids; sql 2306 "INSERT INTO r_1 (id, title, gid) VALUES (99999, 'direct', 1); SELECT COUNT(*) FROM r_1 WHERE id=99999"
––– output –––
{"items":[],"current_line":30,"skipped_lines":0,"errors":false,"error":"","error_code":"","shared_state":"staged"} HTTP 200
ERROR 1064 (42000) at line 1: shared bulk_import into table 'r' is open or failed; commit it or use OPTION clear_sessions=1 to cancel it
children=2
